{
  "schema": 2,
  "mod": "arkonessentials",
  "namespace": "arkonessentials",
  "notes": "Declared permission surface, for permission managers and launchers. 'node' is the dotted form permission mods grant; 'id' is the namespaced identifier the mod checks. 'default' is what applies when nothing grants or denies the node: public = allowed, operator = granted or op level, config = taken from the named setting, denied = only an explicit grant. 'kind' separates modes (mutually exclusive states), abilities, values (config-backed, carrying a number or flag rather than a yes/no), immunities (protections with no operator fallback) and grants. 'parent' is UI nesting and is declared, not derived from dots; 'inheritsFrom' is the dotted ancestor a permission mod would grant to turn this on, which is a different and purely lexical relationship.",
